# What the build context leaves out. The context is the project root
# (docker/lib.sh runs `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .`). It lives at the
# root, not beside the Dockerfile as Dockerfile.dockerignore, because only
# BuildKit reads that name: the legacy builder still in use on some hosts reads
# only this one, and would otherwise send data/ and config.yaml into the build.
.git
.gitignore
.run/
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# The secret key, and this deployment's settings: never in an image layer,
# which is forever. Both are mounted at run time (docker/run.sh).
config/config.yaml
config/secret.key
**/secret.key
**/secret.key.*
config/config.yaml.*
config/.config.yaml.*
*.md
docker/
scripts/
misc/
app/core/layout_pinned.py
app/build_info.py
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
# The JS tests run from the checkout, not in the image.
tests/
